      "verifiedIndependently": "Nothing here was taken from a verdict, so everything was derived from the live board and the rows before being written. Reachability was computed as a transitive closure over every task and bug record on the board, not spot-checked: 19 declared consumers, 16 reachable, 3 not. The three unreachable ones were then read for whether the edge is semantically real rather than merely convenient — TASK-260715-29ws8l AC2 and AC4 require it to specify 'App Group and providerConfiguration data' and 'Keychain accessibility, access group', which are exactly what rules G4 and K2 decide, and it already blocks TASK-260715-1o9wjz and TASK-260715-3f4lxy, so one edge is both correct and sufficient. The new edge was checked for cycles over the whole graph before being added. For N1 the counts were RECOMPUTED rather than trusted: macos.host authors five keys (NE, system-extension.install, app-sandbox, network.client, the Sparkle mach-lookup exception) and the toolchain injects three on development and two on developer-id, so eight and seven are correct at r9 — but §9.1's own text records this number reading 'seven' over a list of ten at r3 and 'nine' at r4, which is why it is now derived instead of written.",
