      "summary": "One authorization-contract correction. No entitlement decision changed, no target row moved, and the authorized mutation set is identical to r6. F1: Ceremony C1's board scope named the superseded revision 2026-07-28.r5, which verdict 05 had rejected, so the human authorization node named by AC5 and by humanAuthorizationNode asked the operator to approve a rejected revision. The board scope now names the current revision, and the DEFECT CLASS is closed rather than the label patched: new object authorizationNodeContract (rule A1) pins the authorization edge the way rule P1 pins the mutation edge, its revisionPinRule derives the banned superseded set from revisionLog so it cannot fall behind a bump, the r6 board gate is extended from one live consumer to BOTH consumers this contract names, new gate R34 checks the A1 pin and the revision bookkeeping, and amendmentRule now requires every future amendment to re-point both pinned board consumers. The gate gained board-level negative gates driven by a simulated board record, so a stale revision, a dropped App ID and a lost exclusion are each proven to fail closed without mutating the board. The rationale's stale check-portal-consumer.sh reference is corrected to .py.",
      "verifiedIndependently": "The finding was re-checked before being accepted, and then widened. The reviewer's jq freshness gate was re-run against r6 and returned false, exit 1, exactly as reported. The C1 record was then checked field by field against c1AuthorizationScope independently of the reviewer's claim that it matched: all four authorized App IDs are named with a right boundary, the Network Extensions and Mac Development wording is present, and all four iOS App IDs plus works.relux.proxy appear only inside a negation - so the revision label was indeed the only defect, and the mutation set must be preserved, not rewritten. CONFIRMED. The class was then swept rather than assumed bounded: all 402 live board elements were scanned for a matrix revision label, which found exactly two - TASK-260728-q5kjta's scope, the reviewer's finding, and this task's own notes field, which the reviewer did not report. The second is NOT a defect: notes is append-only progress history where 'r5 (2026-07-28.r5) closes all three verdict-04 findings' is a true historical statement, the same reason rule S1 excludes revisionLog from its count scan. That distinction is why A1's boardGate declares excludedFields rather than scanning every field, and the sweep is why A1 can state that no third live consumer carries a revision label.",
