        "governedBy": "K3",
        "reason": "The macOS provider reads and writes the file-based System keychain, which is the credential transport TASK-260728-7ii1xz selected. On macOS 26.5 the base App Sandbox profile already grants that path to Network Extension processes and no exception is needed. On the macOS 15.0 floor the grant is unverified.",
        "armingCondition": "Evidence from TASK-260715-1uxx3i that the base App Sandbox profile on the oldest supported macOS does NOT grant /Library/Keychains read and write to a process holding com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension. Nothing else arms it - not a shipping third-party bundle carrying the key, not a runtime failure with another explanation, and not convenience.",
        "armedBy": "TASK-260715-1uxx3i",
        "reviewedIn": "2026-07-28.r10",
        "scopeIfArmed": "macos.provider only, on its two macOS channels. It is granted to no host, no iOS target, and no probe target: no other target opens the System keychain, and the probe family handles no credentials at all.",
        "portalCapability": false
