          "boundKind": "derived-introducing-revision",
          "derivedFrom": "exceptionReviewProvenance (rule X1-P): the revision in which this entry first appears in the digest-pinned snapshot chain, cross-checked against revisionLog[].introduces",
          "whyNotACopy": "reviewedIn is the claim that makes the entry pre-authorized rather than merely written down, so it is derived from evidence OLDER than the claim. X1-C1 is absent from the r8 and r9 snapshots and present in r10, which is a fact about attached files rather than about this one; moving the label to r2 - verdict 10's control - now fails on the chain however many places inside this contract agree with it. r11 bounded the field to membership in the issued revision set, which catches a revision that never existed and not the verdict-06 stale-label class it was written to catch.",
          "supersededBound": "r11's known-revision bound, and the Stated bound paragraph that recorded its gap. Kept here because the gate now REFUSES the old bound kind by name, and a reader who finds known-revision in a diff should find why it was rejected next to it."
