          "rationale": "Withheld under rule G4: the probe's own contract names no shared-container function. TASK-260715-1jckn0 scopes the disposable iOS probe to NETunnelProviderManager save, load, enable, start, status, app-message and stop, one provider protocol and a versioned response, and a clean stop; its AC3 puts the entire host-to-provider exchange on app messaging, which needs no App Group. The r4 rationale said the probe 'exercises the same shared-container path production depends on', but the path the probe actually exercises is sendProviderMessage, and G4 tests a mechanism currently selected on THIS target, never one inherited from the target it resembles. Granting it would make a disposable probe carry an entitlement it never calls and would put an App Group record into circulation with no reader.",
