    "appGroupNote": "r5: Ceremony C1 creates NO App Group record and enables the App Groups capability on NO App ID. Rule G4 prohibits com.apple.security.application-groups on every macOS target, so no C1-authorized App ID needs it. Only ONE App Group record now exists in this contract, group.works.relux.tunnel, whose consumers are the two production iOS App IDs that C1 explicitly does not authorize; it is allocated when iOS re-arms under ADR-024. The probe record was deleted in r5 when the iOS probe pair lost the entitlement (verdict 04 F3).",
    "keychainNote": "r5: C1 authorizes NO Keychain access group mutation, and never did require one - keychain sharing has no portal record (keychainAccessGroups[].portalNote). Rule K2 additionally removes the group from macos.host, so no C1-authorized App ID declares keychain-access-groups at all. An operator asked to 'create the Keychain access group' at C1 is being asked for a mutation that does not exist."
