  "keychainSandboxFloorRule": {
    "id": "K3",
    "statement": "The conclusion that the macOS provider needs no keychain-related entitlement rests on a BASE OS SANDBOX GRANT, which is an OS-version-scoped fact about the running system rather than an invariant of this contract. It holds on the OS versions where it has actually been read. On any supported version below that it is UNVERIFIED, and this contract models it as unresolved instead of settling it by silence.",
    "verifiedOn": "macOS 26.5 (25F71). /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb lines 792-793 grant file-read* and file-write* on the /Library/Keychains subpath to any process holding com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension, and lines 655-656 allow the com.apple.securityd.xpc and com.apple.SecurityServer Mach lookups unconditionally. Re-read and confirmed unchanged for r10.",
    "unverifiedAtFloor": "macOS 15.0 - the binding deployment floor for generated targets, set by .spec/platform-distribution.md 'Minimum platform policy' and selected exactly in .research/260720_task-260715-3r0993-project-generator-deployment-target-policy.md, which also names macos-15 as the minimum hosted CI lane. No macOS 15 host, virtual machine, installer, or SDK-resident sandbox profile exists in this task's environment - only Xcode 26.5 and macOS 26 SDKs - so the floor profile could not be read here. Apple does not document application.sb contents, so no secondary source closes it either. This is a stated gap, not an inference.",
    "whyItMatters": "This matrix is the source for generated entitlements and for the automated allowlist checks. If the floor's base profile does NOT carry the grant, the provider needs a temporary FILE EXCEPTION to reach the System-keychain transport TASK-260728-7ii1xz selected. With no model for that case, the required exception would be rejected as an unreviewed relaxation under rule X1 and assertion A10a, on a supported OS - a silent rejection of a real requirement. Reviewer verdict 08 F1.",
    "resolutionOwner": "TASK-260715-1uxx3i - it already owns the credential-free Apple build matrix whose minimum-macOS lane runs on the macos-15 hosted runner, and reading /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb there is a credential-free static read squarely inside its AC2 static checks. No board element is created for this: the floor lane already exists, and it already reaches this contract transitively through TASK-260715-uyju7n on the live board.",
    "runtimeConsumer": "TASK-260715-1o9wjz - the provider-context resolver whose macOS path actually opens the System keychain. Its provider-context tests are where an absent grant surfaces as a runtime failure rather than as a build finding, so it is the second place the answer lands.",
    "ifGrantAbsentAtFloor": "Arm register entry X1-C1: com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.absolute-path.read-write valued /Library/Keychains/ on macos.provider only, on its two macOS channels. Arming is PRE-AUTHORIZED by this revision, so the exception is a reviewed one the moment the evidence exists and is never an unreviewed relaxation under rule X1 - the review is recorded here, the evidence belongs to the owner. It is an amendment under section 11 that moves the row status and the register entry and changes nothing else.",
    "ifGrantPresentAtFloor": "Record the floor evidence against this rule and retire entry X1-C1. The macos.provider keychain decision then needs no further change: the row stays prohibited under rule K1, on the reason K1 already gives.",
    "notAPortalCapability": "A temporary file exception is a signing-time App Sandbox entitlement. It is not an App ID capability, carries no portal record, and cannot be created or authorized in the Developer portal. Arming it therefore adds nothing to Ceremony C1, whose authorized entries stay exactly as c1AuthorizationScope states them.",
    "ceremonyC1Impact": "none",
    "productEvidenceIsNotProof": "Re-read on this Mac for r10. Surfshark's packet-tunnel system extension declares LSMinimumSystemVersion 10.15 and ships com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.absolute-path.read-write covering /private/var/db/mds/, /Library/Keychains/ and a further private path; PureVPN's two providers declare 10.15 and carry keychain-access-groups; Tailscale's declares 12.4 and carries no keychain entitlement at all. A support range opening at 10.15 spans OS versions this project does not support, and a bundled defensive path set is not a targeted floor fix, so none of the three establishes either necessity or redundancy at macOS 15.0. Rule K1's clause runs in both directions here: a key present in a shipping bundle is not proof the mechanism functions, and a key absent from one is not proof it is unnecessary.",
    "source": "Reviewer verdict 08 F1. /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb on macOS 26.5 (25F71); .spec/platform-distribution.md minimum platform policy; Apple TN3137."
  }
}

